# Certification artifacts, generated by `npm run certify`.
#
# Not committed, deliberately. A stored verdict goes stale the moment the next
# commit lands: release/manifest.json spent this repository's history claiming
# "certification": "VERIFIED" for commit 5680941 — an object that is not in this
# repository at all — over evidence files that said FAILED, with
# BUILD_HASH_PLACEHOLDER in place of a build hash and a CycloneDX SBOM listing
# zero components. None of it could be checked, because none of it was measured.
#
# Evidence is now produced at a known commit by scripts/certify.mjs, verified by
# scripts/verify-evidence.mjs, and uploaded by CI as a build artifact. An absent
# release/ means uncertified, which is honest and true of any fresh checkout.
release/
